G1223.def:
**διά** (before a vowel δ᾽, exc. [[Rom.8.10|Rom.8:10]], [[2Co.5.7|2Co.5:7]], and in (Proper name)s; Tdf., _Pr._, 94),
_prep. with genitive, accusative, as in cl.; _
1. with genitive, **through**;
(i) **of Place, after verbs of motion or action**: [[Mat.2.12; 12.43|Mat.2:12 12:43]], [[Mrk.2.23|Mrk.2:23]], [[Luk.4.30|Luk.4:30]], [[Jhn.4.4|Jhn.4:4]], [[2Co.11.33|2Co.11:33]], al.; σώζεσθαι (διας-) δ. πυρός, ὕδατος, [[1Co.3.15|1Co.3:15]], [[1Pe.3.20|1Pe.3:20]]; βλέπειν δ. ἐσόπτρου, [[1Co.13.12|1Co.13:12]] metaphorically, of a state or condition: [[Rom.14.20|Rom.14:20]], [[2Co.2.4; 5.7|2Co.2:4 5:7]], 10; δ. γράμματος, ἀκροβυστίας (Lft., _Notes_, 263, 279), [[Rom.2.27; 4.11|Rom.2:27 4:11]]; δι ̓ὑπομενῆς, [[Rom.8.25|Rom.8:25]]
(ii) **Of Time**;
(a) **during which**: [[Mat.26.61|Mat.26:61]], [[Mrk.14.58|Mrk.14:58]], [[Luk.5.5|Luk.5:5]]; δ. παντὸς τοῦ ζῆν, [[Heb.2.15|Heb.2:15]] δ. παντός (διαπαντός in [[Mrk.5.5|Mrk.5:5]], [[Luk.24.53|Luk.24:53]]), **always, continually**, [[Mat.18.10|Mat.18:10]], [[Act.2.25|Act.2:25]]" (LXX) 10:2 24:16, [[Rom.11.10|Rom.11:10]]" (LXX), [[2Th.3.16|2Th.3:16]], [[Heb.9.6; 13.15|Heb.9:6 13:15]].
(b) **within which**: [[Act.1.3|Act.1:3]] δ. νυκτός, [[Act.5.19; 16.9; 17.10; 23.31|Act.5:19 16:9 17:10 23:31]];
(with) **after which **(Field, _Notes_, 20; Abbott, _JG_, 255f.): [[Mrk.2.1|Mrk.2:1]], [[Act.24.17|Act.24:17]], [[Gal.2.1|Gal.2:1]].
(iii) **Of the Means or Instrument**;
(1) **of the efficient cause **(regarded also as the instrument): of God, [[Rom.11.36|Rom.11:36]], [[1Co.1.9|1Co.1:9]], [[Gal.4.7|Gal.4:7]], [[Heb.2.10; 7.21|Heb.2:10 7:21]]; of Christ, [[Rom.1.8; 5.1, 17|Rom.1:8 5:1, 17]], [[1Co.15.21|1Co.15:21]], [[1Pe.4.11|1Pe.4:11]], al.; δ. τ. ὑμῶν δεήσεως, [[Rom.1.12|Rom.1:12]], [[2Co.1.4|2Co.1:4]], [[Gal.4.23|Gal.4:23]], al.;
(2) **of the agent, instrument or means**;
(a) with genitive of person(s), [[Mat.11.2|Mat.11:2]], [[Luk.1.70|Luk.1:70]], [[Jhn.1.17|Jhn.1:17]], [[Act.1.16|Act.1:16]], [[Rom.2.16|Rom.2:16]], [[1Co.1.21|1Co.1:21]], [[Eph.1.5|Eph.1:5]], [[Heb.2.14|Heb.2:14]], [[Rev.1.1|Rev.1:1]], al.; ὑπὸ τ. κυρίου δ. τ. προφήτου (δ. τ. κυρίου, [[1Th.4.2|1Th.4:2]] (M, _Th._, in l.); Lft., _Rev._, 121f.), [[Mat.1.22; 2.15|Mat.1:22 2:15]], [[Rom.1.2|Rom.1:2]]; δ. ἐπιστολῆς ὡς δ. ἡμῶν (Field, _Notes_, 202), [[2Th.2.2|2Th.2:2]] δ. Σ. (_NTD_, 22), [[1Pe.5.12|1Pe.5:12]]
(b) with genitive of thing(s) (where often the simple dative is used in cl.; Jannaris, _Gr._, 375), [[Jhn.11.4|Jhn.11:4]], [[Act.5.12|Act.5:12]]; δ. τ. πίστεως, [[Rom.3.30|Rom.3:30]] δ. λόγου θεοῦ, [[1Pe.1.23|1Pe.1:23]] δ. παραβολῆς, [[Luk.8.4|Luk.8:4]] δουλεύειν δ. τ. ἀγάπης, [[Gal.5.13|Gal.5:13]] δ. ἐπαγγελίας, [[Gal.3.18|Gal.3:18]],
2. C. accusative;
(i) rarely, as with genitive, **through** (Hom), δ. μέσον Σαμαρίας (ICC, in l.; Bl., §42, 1; Robertson, _Gr._, 581), [[Luk.17.11|Luk.17:11]]
(ii) **by reason of, because of, for the sake of**;
(a) with accusative of person(s) (M, _Pr._, 105), [[Mrk.2.27|Mrk.2:27]], [[Jhn.6.57; 11.42|Jhn.6:57 11:42]], [[Rom.8.20|Rom.8:20]];
(b) with accusative of thing(s), δ. φθόνον, [[Mat.27.18|Mat.27:18]], [[Mrk.15.10|Mrk.15:10]]; δ. φόβον, [[Jhn.7.13; 20.19|Jhn.7:13 20:19]]; δ. ἀγάπην, [[Eph.2.4|Eph.2:4]] δ. τοῦτο, freq., **for this cause, therefore**, [[Mat.6.25|Mat.6:25]], [[Mrk.6.14|Mrk.6:14]], [[Luk.11.49|Luk.11:49]], [[Jhn.6.65|Jhn.6:65]], al.; id. before ὅτι, [[Jhn.5.16; 10.17|Jhn.5:16 10:17]], al.; δ. τί, **why**, [[Mat.9.11, 14|Mat.9:11, 14]] [[Mrk.2.18|Mrk.2:18]], [[Jhn.7.45|Jhn.7:45]], al.; δ. τό, with inf., [[Mrk.5.4|Mrk.5:4]], [[Luk.9.7|Luk.9:7]], [[Jas.4.2|Jas.4:2]].
3. In composition,
(1) **through**, as in διαβαίνω;
(2) of separation, **asunder**, as in διασπάω;
(3) of distribution, **abroad**, as in διαγγέλλω;
(4) **of transition, as διαλλάσσω**;
(5) of "perfective" action (M, _Pr._, 112f., 115f.), as διαφύγω, διακαθαρίζω.
(AS)

G1228.def:
**διάβολος**, -ον
(διαβάλλω, which see) [in LXX for שָׂטָן (as [[Job.1.6|Job.1:6]]), exc. [[Est.7.4; 8.1|Est.7:4 8:1]] (צַר, צָרַר) ;]
**slanderous, accusing falsely**. As subst., ὁ, ἡ, δ.;
(a) generally (of. Es, ll. with), **a slanderer, false accuser**: [[1Ti.3.6|1Ti.3:6]], 7 (CGT, in l., but see infr.) 3:11, [[2Ti.3.3|2Ti.3:3]], [[Tit.2.3|Tit.2:3]];
(b) **as chiefly in LXX, of Satan, the Accuser, the Devil**: [[Mat.4.1, 5, 8, 11; 13.39; 25.41|Mat.4:1, 5, 8, 11 13:39 25:41]], [[Luk.4.2, 3, 6, 13; 8.12|Luk.4:2, 3, 6, 13 8:12]], [[Jhn.13.2|Jhn.13:2]], [[Act.10.38|Act.10:38]], [[Eph.4.27; 6.11|Eph.4:27 6:11]], [[1Ti.3.6|1Ti.3:6]], 7 (but see supr.), [[2Ti.2.26|2Ti.2:26]], [[Heb.2.14|Heb.2:14]], [[Jas.4.7|Jas.4:7]], [[1Pe.5.8|1Pe.5:8]], [[Jude.9|Ju 9]], [[Rev.2.10; 12.9, 12; 20.2, 10|Rev.2:10 12:9, 12 20:2, 10]]; εἶναι ἐκ τοῦ δ., [[Jhn.8.44|Jhn.8:44]], [[1Jn.3.8|1Jn.3:8]]; τέκνα τοῦ δ., [[1Jn.3.10|1Jn.3:10]] υἱὸς, [[Act.13.10|Act.13:10]] metaphorically, of Judas, [[Jhn.6.70|Jhn.6:70]] (Cremer, 121; _DCG_, ii, 605).†
(AS)

G1219.def:
**δημόσιος**, -α, -ον
(δῆμος), [in LXX: [[2Ma.6.10|2Ma.6:10]], [[3Ma.2.27; 4.7|3Ma.2:27 4:7]] * ;]
**belonging to the people, public**: [[Act.5.18|Act.5:18]] dative fem. used adverbially (cl.);
(a) **at the public expense, by public consent**;
(b) **publicly**: [[Act.16.37; 18.28; 20.20|Act.16:37 18:28 20:20]].†
(AS)
